%rec: Home
%doc: This archive's identity: one per home catalogue, made by arv init (or on first use).
+ Each home is its own privacy sphere: a disc carries the catalogue of its home only, and
+ names it (HomeUuid in catalog.rec). A home rebuilt from a disc keeps the disc's Uuid;
+ arv rebuild refuses a disc of another home unless told otherwise. Name is for people.
%key: Uuid
%mandatory: Uuid
%type: Uuid uuid
%type: Date date

Uuid: UUID
Date: 2026-01-01

%rec: Disc
%doc: One record per physical disc image (an OAIS AIP). Field names follow
+ Dublin Core terms where one fits: Title, Creator, Date, Description,
+ Subject, Coverage, Rights. Uuid is the machine identity of the image
+ (copies burned from one image share it); Id is for people and is
+ derived from Set, Sequence and Coverage (EDTF) under IdScheme, so it
+ can always be regenerated and checked (see docs/spec/smart-archive-format.md).
%key: Id
%mandatory: Id Title Date
%type: Uuid uuid
%type: Sequence int
%type: Date date
%type: Files int
%type: Bytes int
%type: Access enum public private sealed
%type: Retired date

Id: CODE-01_2020_0
Uuid: UUID
IdScheme: set-seq-coverage/1
Label: CODE-01_2020_0 T"x
Title: T"x
Set: CODE
Path: PROJECTS/CODE
Sequence: 1
Coverage: 2020
Date: 2026-01-01
Creator: Sam
Description: Line, with "quotes"
Subject: one
Subject: two
Access: private
Rights: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Files: 3
Bytes: 20
Software: SW

%rec: Binding
%doc: How one volume is stored on its medium: the container (filesystem) and the
+ protection (error correction) it was made with. These change with the medium;
+ the files and the rest of the catalogue do not (research/plan.md, four layers).
+ Container: iso9660+udf-1.02, udf-2.50 (later perhaps ltfs, exfat, tar, afs).
+ Protection: rs03 or none. Media, Filesystem and Ecc describe them for people
+ (format 0.2 and earlier kept those three in the Disc record).
%key: Volume
%mandatory: Volume Container Protection
%type: MediumSectors int

Volume: CODE-01_2020_0
Container: udf-2.50
Protection: none
Media: M-DISC BD-R 25GB
Filesystem: UDF 2.50, BD-ROM layout with metadata partition and a real mirror (arv udfwrite)
Ecc: none
ImageSectors: 850
ImageSha256: SHA256

%rec: Event
%doc: Preservation actions and metadata changes, appended and never edited. Type uses
+ the PREMIS eventType vocabulary: https://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/preservation/eventType
+ Disc names the disc; a change to a location or a selection names it in Object
+ (location:CODE, selection:CODE) instead.
+ Agent (one or more) is software (arv@COMMIT), a model (llm:MODEL, embeddings:MODEL) or a person (human:LOGIN).
+ Authorship says how people and machines shared the work: automatic (software
+ following rules), suggested (a model, not reviewed), accepted (a model's suggestion
+ a person kept as it was), edited (one a person changed), human (a person alone).
+ A replication records one copy: Form (disc, iso: the image as a file, folder: the disc's
+ files), Temperature (hot, warm, cold: given, else its place's, else cold for a disc and
+ warm for a file or folder), Path for a file or folder; with ReadBack: identical it is a copy read back against its image before it
+ was recorded (known good); deaccession retires a disc (its Disc record gets Retired).
%mandatory: Type Date Outcome
%type: Outcome enum success failure warning
%type: Authorship enum automatic suggested accepted edited human

Disc: CODE-01_2020_0
Type: message digest calculation
Date: 2026-01-01
Outcome: success
Authorship: automatic
Agent: SW
Note: sha256 and sha512 manifests of 3 files

Disc: CODE-01_2020_0
Type: creation
Date: 2026-01-01
Outcome: success
Authorship: automatic
Agent: SW
Note: image CODE-01_2020_0.noecc.iso, 850 sectors
